 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** An octree structure storing scalar values at voxel centers. The octree represents a volume where each leaf node contains a single scalar datum $v$.
-*   **Output:** Intersection points with an isosurface defined within cells formed by 8 adjacent voxels.
